## Oil and fluid services

- Engine oil changes
- Transmission fluid services
- Coolant and antifreeze services
- Power steering fluid checks
- Differential fluid changes
- Hydraulic fluid maintenance
- Brake fluid inspections

## Why the interval matters

Fresh oil lubricates, carries heat away and keeps what it picks up in
suspension. Old oil does none of those three well, and the sludge that follows
costs an engine long before anyone sees a warning. Staying on the interval is
the cheapest maintenance decision available on a diesel.

Oil is the one everybody tracks. Transmission fluid, coolant, power steering,
brake and differential fluid are the ones that fail quietly — we check the level
and the condition of each, because a fluid at the right level can still be
finished.

